// v3.std.coproduct_projection — Variant-aware projection metadata
// carrier for coproduct response bodies.
//
// Substrate-fact-introduction (P1 procedure) per
// `docs/briefs/r3-substrate-s5-coproduct-projection-carrier-worker.md`,
// Director γ-ratification at gunb-ai/gunbc#828 c#4394369848. Closure
// predicate: §1.8 gates #29-#30 (T-Anthropic-Wire). Unblocks Anthropic
// Messages #1702 re-dispatch + the three already-briefed coproduct
// paydowns (`r3-coproduct-{1,2,3}-*-worker.md`).
//
// **Layering**: compiler-internal projection substrate, NOT user-facing
// language vocabulary. Contrast `dsl/std/serialization.dag::CoproductWireContract`
// which lives in `dsl/std/` because users declare wire contracts.
// `CoproductProjection` is consumed by the projection-resolver during
// REST-response coproduct dispatch — the `from`-path resolver reads
// this carrier instead of a `response_variant_tag: String` shim.
//
// **Single-keyed-fact discipline (P2 boundary)**: per-variant payload +
// tag-value live as one keyed fact (`CoproductVariantProjection`), not
// two parallel maps. A variant cannot have a field projection without a
// wire-tag value or vice versa — illegal-state-by-construction.
//
// **Path-(a) shape decision** (Director ratified #4400354502 over (b)
// `FieldRef` introduction): `wire_tag_field: String`, with structural
// identity carried by the `Map<VariantId, CoproductVariantProjection>`
// key invariant + per-variant typed `WireTagValue`. Aligns with the
// `services.dag:28-36` precedent that explicitly rejects parallel
// field-handle wrappers ("`InputFieldRef` … would duplicate without
// strengthening the structural invariant"). Fail-closed boundary
// check at fixture load validates `wire_tag_field` names a real field
// on the coproduct's variant payloads.
//
// **DeclarationRef alias debt** (Director-pre-ratified observation #1
// disposition (b)): `DeclarationRef = String` alias accepted for this
// slice; debt-paydown row landed in
// `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md` naming the carrier
// + 2-clause OR-trigger (audit-row #14 closure OR string-identity
// bridge surfaces on a `DeclarationRef`-typed consumer). Promotes to
// structural typed shape on trigger fire.

module v3.std.coproduct_projection

// `DeclarationRef` resolves to `dsl/std/serialization.dag:16`'s
// `DeclarationRef = String` alias — the soft-typed nominal handle
// the brief + Director's path-(a) ratification reference. This is
// distinct from the `type DeclarationRef {}` empty record at
// `src/v3/spec/v3_l1.dag:76` (a separate identity declared for the
// v3 spec layer); the two-co-existing-`DeclarationRef`-types is a
// pre-existing P2 single-authority concern surfaced by Mgr review
// at gunb-ai/gunbc#2164 and tracked separately (likely folds into
// audit-row #14's module-convergence dissolution trigger). The
// debt-paydown row at `docs/debt/r3-debt-paydown-ledger-2026-05-02.md`
// names the `String` alias (this import) for promotion; both
// `DeclarationRef`s dissolve together when convergence lands.
import std.serialization { DeclarationRef }

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD. String-aliased variant identity handle. Keys
// `CoproductProjection.variant_projections` and `WireTagValue` payloads.
// Today's substrate grammar can't express a refined
// `DeclarationRef<VariantDeclaration>`; keying by string mirrors the
// `DeclarationRef = String` alias precedent at
// `dsl/std/serialization.dag:16` and the same disposition (b) per
// Director #4394416049. **Dissolution trigger** (paired with the
// `DeclarationRef` debt row): promotes to a structural typed handle
// (e.g., `(coproduct: DeclarationRef, name: String)`) when EITHER
// (a) audit-row #14 closes module-convergence OR (b) a `VariantId`-
// typed consumer surfaces a string-identity bridge per
// `feedback_opaque_strings_attract_heuristics`.
type VariantId = String

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD coproduct (single-arm record at PR-α scope). Typed leaf
// for per-variant wire-tag values. Anthropic + REST both string-
// serialize tags at the wire boundary; the typed-on-our-side /
// serialized-at-emit pattern keeps the substrate value distinct from
// its String wire form. Single `StringTag` arm at this slice covers
// the closure-predicate consumers (Anthropic #1702 + the three
// coproduct paydowns); additional arms (e.g., `IntTag`, `EnumTag`)
// land additively when a wire surface needs them. Dissolution trigger:
// none — this stays SCAFFOLD until all ratifications close, at which
// point it earns a TERMINAL receipt. Brief constraint #2 binding:
// `WireTagValue` MUST stay a typed leaf, NOT collapse to `String`.
type WireTagValue
  = StringTag { value: String }

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Per-field metadata slot inside a variant's
// payload projection. Empty in PR-α because the projection-resolver
// keys variant dispatch by tag-value alone today; reserved as a record
// so PR-β can grow `ty: …` / `wire_name: …` without changing
// `FieldProjection.Fields.fields`'s map shape. Mirrors the
// `services.dag::InputField {}` precedent at `:64`: canonical name held
// by the enclosing `Map<String, FieldShape>` key, no `name: String`
// duplication.
type FieldShape {}

// 🟡 SCAFFOLD coproduct. Per-variant payload field projection. `Empty`
// constructor encodes "variant has no payload fields" (e.g., Anthropic
// empty-payload variants per brief §"Single-keyed-fact discipline")
// without representing absence as a missing map entry — keeps
// illegal-state-by-construction. `Fields` carries the populated case
// keyed by field name (uniqueness by `Map` key invariant; same
// boundary discipline as `Operation.inputs` at `services.dag:28-36`).
// Dissolution trigger: when the projection-resolver consumes typed
// field shapes (rather than name-only dispatch), `FieldShape {}` grows
// concrete fields and a TERMINAL receipt lands.
type FieldProjection
  = Empty
  | Fields { fields: Map<String, FieldShape> }

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Single keyed fact (P2 boundary): a
// variant's payload projection and its wire-tag value live together.
// Splitting into parallel `Map<VariantId, FieldProjection>` +
// `Map<VariantId, WireTagValue>` would admit a variant with a tag but
// no field projection (or vice versa) as structurally representable
// — per Director's openai-pro REQUEST_CHANGES correction at PR #2079.
type CoproductVariantProjection {
  field_projection: FieldProjection
  wire_tag_value:   WireTagValue
}

// 🟢 TERMINAL at PR-α scope. Top-level projection carrier keyed by the
// coproduct declaration. `wire_tag_field: String` per path-(a) ratified
// shape (Director #4400354502): structural identity via the
// `variant_projections` map key invariant + per-variant typed
// `WireTagValue`; fail-closed fixture-load check validates that
// `wire_tag_field` names a real field on the coproduct's variant
// payloads (analogous to `services.dag` PR-β `ParamToken.name → Map<
// String, InputField>` key validation).
//
// `declaration: DeclarationRef` carries the `DeclarationRef = String`
// alias soft-typed handle per Director observation #1 disposition (b);
// debt-paydown row tracks promotion to structural typed shape.
//
// Asymmetry with `InternallyTaggedObject.tag_field: String` at
// `dsl/std/serialization.dag:49` collapses under path (a) — both
// String, no debt row needed (brief §3 conditional debt does not fire).
type CoproductProjection {
  declaration:         DeclarationRef
  wire_tag_field:      String
  variant_projections: Map<VariantId, CoproductVariantProjection>
}
